issues.suggestion:
Add an M-current gating variable p with slow sigmoid kinetics. In the kinetics block add:
  def p_inf(x): return 1.0 / (1.0 + Exp(-(x - param_i) / 10.0))
  def tau_p(x): return torch.clamp(-param_j / (3.3 * (Exp((x - param_i) / 40.0) + Exp(-(x - param_i) / 20.0))), min=10.0, max=2000.0)
Declare state variable: p = torch.zeros((batch_size, time_steps), device=device)
Initialize: p[:, 0] = p_inf(V[:, 0])
In the loop, compute p_inf and tau_p at V[:,i-1], then add to tau_V_inv: + gbar_X1 * p[:,i-1], and to V_inf numerator: + gbar_X1 * p[:,i-1] * E_K. Update state: p[:,i] = p_inf(V[:,i-1]) + (p[:,i-1] - p_inf(V[:,i-1])) * Exp(-tstep / tau_p(V[:,i-1])). This uses gbar_X1 (conductance), param_i (half-activation voltage, negated to negative mV), and param_j (time constant scaling, negated to negative large value matching slow M-current ~100–500 ms range).
